 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Diabetic Retinopathy Grading: Gemini vs. MedGemma vs. RetiZero\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is a working driver for the project's experiments. It: \n",
    "- prepares a small test metadata CSV (if missing),\n",
    "- runs the three adapter scripts (`src/run_gemini.py`, `src/run_medgemma.py`, `src/run_retizero.py`) in either `--mock` or real mode,\n",
    "- computes evaluation metrics and confusion matrices, and\n",
    "- writes a clearly-labeled final report `reports/final_report.md`.\n",
    "\n",
    "IMPORTANT: the notebook guards against automatically installing large packages or downloading heavy weights. Use `--mock` for safe CI runs. To run real models, set the required secrets and weights as documented in README."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# 0. Safe environment & paths (no heavy installs run automatically)\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os\n",
    "ROOT = Path('.')\n",
    "RESULTS_DIR = ROOT / 'results'\n",
    "REPORTS_DIR = ROOT / 'reports'\n",
    "TESTS_DIR = ROOT / 'tests'\n",
    "RESULTS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "REPORTS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "TESTS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print('Paths ready:', RESULTS_DIR, REPORTS_DIR, TESTS_DIR)"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install minimal dependencies (mock & reporting)\n",
    "Run the cell below to install lightweight packages used for reporting and metrics. This will NOT install model-weight-heavy packages (torch, transformers) — those are only needed for real runs and are installed manually when you opt in.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you are in CI or want a fully offline safe run, use `--mock` mode when calling the adapters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# Install minimal packages for metrics and plotting\n",
    "import sys, subprocess\n",
    "def safe_install(pkgs):\n",
    "    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '--upgrade', 'pip'])\n",
    "    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install'] + pkgs)\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import pandas as pd\n",
    "    import sklearn\n",
    "    import matplotlib\n",
    "    import seaborn as sns\n",
    "except Exception:\n",
    "    print('Installing lightweight packages: pandas scikit-learn matplotlib seaborn')\n",
    "    safe_install(['pandas','scikit-learn','matplotlib','seaborn'])\n",
    "    import pandas as pd\n",
    "    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "    import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Dependencies available')"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Ensure test metadata exists (creates a 125-sample balanced CSV if missing)\n",
    "This creates `tests/test_metadata_subset.csv` with columns `id_code,image_path,diagnosis`. The notebook does NOT include large image files; adapters' mock mode does not require images." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import csv\n",
    "if not (TESTS_DIR / 'test_metadata_subset.csv').exists():\n",
    "    print('Creating tests/test_metadata_subset.csv (125 balanced samples)')\n",
    "    ids = [f'id{n:03d}' for n in range(125)]\n",
    "    diagnoses = [g for g in range(5) for _ in range(25)]\n",
    "    image_paths = [f'images/{ids[i]}.png' for i in range(125)]\n",
    "    with open(TESTS_DIR / 'test_metadata_subset.csv', 'w', newline='') as f:\n",
    "        writer = csv.writer(f)\n",
    "        writer.writerow(['id_code','image_path','diagnosis'])\n",
    "        for i in range(125):\n",
    "            writer.writerow([ids[i], image_paths[i], diagnoses[i]])\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('Found existing', TESTS_DIR / 'test_metadata_subset.csv')\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Run adapters (mock or real)\n",
    "This notebook provides helper functions to run each adapter script. By default, the cells below call adapters in `--mock` mode to produce deterministic predictions. To run real models, remove `--mock` and ensure you have the required credentials and weights (see README)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import subprocess, shlex, os\n",
    "def run_adapter(script, input_csv, output_csv, mock=True, extra_args=None, env=None):\n",
    "    cmd = [sys.executable, script, '--input', str(input_csv), '--output', str(output_csv)]\n",
    "    if mock:\n",
    "        cmd.append('--mock')\n",
    "    if extra_args:\n",
    "        cmd += extra_args\n",
    "    print('Running:', ' '.join(cmd))\n",
    "    completed = subprocess.run(cmd, env=env or os.environ, capture_output=True, text=True)\n",
    "    print('Return code:', completed.returncode)\n",
    "    if completed.stdout:\n",
    "        print('STDOUT:', completed.stdout[:1000])\n",
    "    if completed.stderr:\n",
    "        print('STDERR:', completed.stderr[:1500])\n",
    "    return completed.returncode == 0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage (mock-safe):\n",
    "input_csv = TESTS_DIR / 'test_metadata_subset.csv'\n",
    "out_csv = RESULTS_DIR / 'predictions.csv'\n",
    "# Run each adapter in mock mode and append/merge outputs into the same predictions.csv\n",
    "# The adapter scripts are expected to either create or append consistent columns ending with '_pred'\n",
    "print('Adapters will run in --mock mode by default. To run real models, set mock=False and ensure credentials/weights are present.')\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3a) Run the three adapters (mock) — single-cell convenience command\n",
    "Run this cell to produce results/predictions.csv using the adapters in `--mock` mode. It overwrites results/predictions.csv." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# Run all three adapters in mock mode and overwrite predictions.csv\n",
    "# They each will write columns gemini_pred, medgemma_pred, retizero_pred\n",
    "mock = True\n",
    "# Remove previous results file if present\n",
    "if (RESULTS_DIR / 'predictions.csv').exists():\n",
    "    (RESULTS_DIR / 'predictions.csv').unlink()\n",
    "# Run Gemini\n",
    "run_adapter('src/run_gemini.py', input_csv, out_csv, mock=mock)\n",
    "# Run MedGemma\n",
    "run_adapter('src/run_medgemma.py', input_csv, out_csv, mock=mock)\n",
    "# Run RetiZero\n",
    "run_adapter('src/run_retizero.py', input_csv, out_csv, mock=mock)\n",
    "print('Adapters finished (mock mode). Check', out_csv)\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Compute metrics and generate a clearly-labeled report\n",
    "This cell reads `results/predictions.csv`, computes Accuracy, QWK, MAE per model, writes `results/metrics.txt`, and updates `reports/final_report.md` with the mock numbers while clearly labeling them as mock/pilot results." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, cohen_kappa_score, mean_absolute_error\n",
    "import textwrap, os\n",
    "pred_path = RESULTS_DIR / 'predictions.csv'\n",
    "if not pred_path.exists():\n",
    "    print('No predictions.csv found at', pred_path)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(pred_path)\n",
    "    models = [c for c in df.columns if c.endswith('_pred')]\n",
    "    lines = []\n",
    "    metrics = {}\n",
    "    for m in models:\n",
    "        valid = df.dropna(subset=[m,'diagnosis']) if 'diagnosis' in df.columns else df.dropna(subset=[m])\n",
    "        if len(valid) == 0 or 'diagnosis' not in df.columns:\n",
    "            lines.append(f"{m}: N=0")\n",
    "            metrics[m] = {'N':0,'Accuracy':None,'QWK':None,'MAE':None}\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        y_true = valid['diagnosis'].astype(int)\n",
    "        y_pred = valid[m].astype(int)\n",
    "        acc = accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "        qwk = cohen_kappa_score(y_true, y_pred, weights='quadratic')\n",
    "        mae = mean_absolute_error(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "        lines.append(f"{m}: N={len(valid)}, Accuracy={acc:.3f}, QWK={qwk:.3f}, MAE={mae:.3f}")\n",
    "        metrics[m] = {'N':len(valid),'Accuracy':round(acc,3),'QWK':round(qwk,3),'MAE':round(mae,3)}\n",
    "    # write metrics file\n",
    "    with open(RESULTS_DIR / 'metrics.txt', 'w') as f:\n",
    "        f.write('\n'.join(lines))\n",
    "    print('Wrote results/metrics.txt')\n",
    "    # Append/update final report: we keep the existing final_report.md and replace the mock summary block if present\n",
    "    report_path = REPORTS_DIR / 'final_report.md'\n",
    "    header = '# Final report — Diabetic Retinopathy VLM Comparison\n'\n",
    "    # Build mock summary block\n",
    "    mock_block = '\n---\n\n## Mock Results (deterministic)\n\nThe repository\'s mock evaluation validates the pipeline and reporting format. These numbers\nare deterministic pseudo-predictions used only to exercise the downstream analysis code —\nthey are NOT real model outputs and must not be used as experimental or clinical claims.\n\nSummary metrics (mock):\n\n'\n",
    "    for m, s in metrics.items():\n",
    "        name = m.replace('_pred','').capitalize()\n",
    "        mock_block += f'- {name} (mock)\n  - N = {s["N"]}\n  - Accuracy = {s["Accuracy"]}\n  - QWK = {s["QWK"]}\n  - MAE = {s["MAE"]}\n\n'\n",
    "    mock_block += '---\n'\n",
    "    # If report exists, read and try to remove previous mock section (naive replace between markers)\n",
    "    if report_path.exists():\n",
    "        text = report_path.read_text()\n",
    "        # Remove any existing '## Mock Results' section (simple heuristic)\n",
    "        import re\n",
    "        text = re.sub(r'---\n\n## Mock Results[\s\S]*?---\n', '', text)\n",
    "        new_text = text + '\n' + mock_block\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # create a simple final report if none exists\n",
    "        new_text = header + '\n' + mock_block\n",
    "    with open(report_path, 'w') as f:\n",
    "        f.write(new_text)\n",
    "    print('Updated', report_path)\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Optional: Generate confusion matrices and plots (if you have real predictions)\n",
    "If `results/predictions.csv` contains `diagnosis` and `<model>_pred` columns, this cell will save confusion matrix images to `results/`." 
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "pred_path = RESULTS_DIR / 'predictions.csv'\n",
    "if pred_path.exists():\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(pred_path)\n",
    "    models = [c for c in df.columns if c.endswith('_pred') and 'diagnosis' in df.columns] if 'diagnosis' in pd.read_csv(pred_path).columns else []\n",
    "    for m in models:\n",
    "        import numpy as np\n",
    "        y_true = df['diagnosis'].astype(int)\n",
    "        y_pred = df[m].astype(int)\n",
    "        from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix\n",
    "        cm = confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred, labels=[0,1,2,3,4])\n",
    "        plt.figure(figsize=(6,5))\n",
    "        sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues')\n",
    "        plt.xlabel('Predicted')\n",
    "        plt.ylabel('True')\n",
    "        plt.title(m.replace('_pred','') + ' confusion matrix')\n",
    "        outfig = RESULTS_DIR / f'{m}_confusion.png'\n",
    "        plt.savefig(outfig, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "        plt.close()\n",
    "        print('Wrote', outfig)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No predictions.csv found; skipping plots')\n"
   ],
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Notes & safe usage\n",
    "- Use `--mock` to run safely in CI or if secrets/weights are not available.\n",
    "- To run real models: ensure `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `HF_TOKEN` are set in your environment (or secrets), and `RETIZERO_WEIGHTS_PATH` points to a usable weights file.\n",
    "- Running real models may install heavy packages (torch, transformers, accelerate). Install them manually in a controlled environment.\n"
   ]
  }
 ]
